  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're on a bit of a role, Supervisor Journey. This Congress probably doesn't get any style points for how we have gotten there. But quietly and sometimes awkwardly over the last six to eight months, we have begun assembling a record of really big deliverables for the American people. So the first gun violence reform we've been able to pass through Congress in 30 years, a huge bipartisan infrastructure bill that became law last November, a major Inflation Reduction Act that lowers prescription drug prices. Also, make sure that healthcare premiums don't spiral out of control in the months ahead because they were set to kind of go off a cliff. And then very importantly, the largest investment in clean energy and climate action that we've ever done. Add to that a bill we call the CHIPS Plus Act, which is to address the supply chain constraint and the fact that we no longer have the world leadership role on semiconductor manufacturing and science and technology in some respects. So it's a huge forward-looking bill. We've passed the largest investment in wildlife restoration and habitat protection, a bill called the Recovering America's Wildlife Act. Some of this has bipartisan support. Most of it has been pretty much Democrats doing all the heavy lifting. But when you add it all up and then couple it with the big one we did out the gate, the American Rescue Plan. which was a huge multi-trillion dollar bill that got emergency relief out to small businesses and families during the depths of the pandemic, had the largest vaccine rollout in world history and most successful, brought the pandemic under control, got the economy out of the ditch. It is a good story to tell and it is translating to a lot of momentum right now for Democrats.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
