    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's true. Now that it was the same in Sacramento at the state level, when you were dealing with water quality, there was a separate committee called environmental safety and toxic control. Yeah, or toxic management, I think it was ESTM. And I chaired that initially. That was water quality, but everything else about water was over in the other committee I chaired. In Congress, it's split up even more. When you're talking about like drinking water standards, that is the EPA Clean Water Act that's over at a large committee called Energy and Commerce. If you're talking about the flood, that is the Corps of Engineers and another part of the Clean Water Act. And that is at the Transportation and Infrastructure Committee, which I serve on. And then when you're talking about water supply, you know, stream flows, the environmental aspects of water, that's the committee, I said subcommittee chair, sorry, water oceans and wildlife.",
