    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, the Klamath is a little bit of a clearer cut because there's no water supply involved in these four hydrodams in the Klamath River. You're just simply dealing with aging obsolete hydrodams that cause terrible water quality and parasite problems that have really wrecked the salmon and steelhead fisheries for downstream tribes that I represent in the fishing community for decades. And it was simply a function of the owner of those dams coming to realize that real licensing them was going to be very expensive and impractical. And probably get that power from renewables and other sources more cheaply and easily. So that was a business decision, thankfully supported by the states of Oregon and California and the federal government and the tribes I represent, all coming together. And the good news there, Dan, is that this time next year, we should be taking out the first of those four dams on the ground, dam removal, largest dam removal, really good news for Lower Klamath River. stakeholders.",
