  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Okay, and just a reminder to our listeners, this is Susan Yu, I'm your host Dan Jurti, first Wednesday of the month, host Marty Roden on the third Wednesday of the month. And this is public radio, minutes, you know, county public radio, KZYX. And today our guest is Jared Huffman. He's an our member of Congress representing us here in the North Coast. Jared, we've seen number of people get appointed to the Supreme Court over recent years, but it was still, I got to say, it was like a punch to the gut when the court overturned Roe versus Roe v. Wade. What do you see that the Biden administration or the House representatives where our state, what can people see as some sort of relief from the unprecedented action by the Supreme Court to disregard nearly 50 years of precedent?",
