  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Most important thing we can do right now, because I know everyone is looking for the quick fix to this scary Supreme Court. You got to elect two new U.S. senators, and you got to hold a Democratic House. If we can do those two things, we can dump the filibuster, and we can legislate in a way that backfills for all of these terrible decisions. So if the Supreme Court says, well, Congress wasn't clear enough to let you regulate You know, carbon pollution in this way. Well, Congress can backfill with more specific legislation. We can do that a lot faster than anything else to address the problem. We can do that to address the Dobbs decision and Roe v. Wade. We can absolutely codify women's reproductive rights. We've already passed that out of the house. We just need to dump the filibuster and it'll pass the Senate. We can codify gay marriage and other things that are probably in the crosshairs of this Supreme Court as well. It's a little trickier on the religious liberty side of it, but many of the things this Supreme Court is doing, the center-stir agenda of theirs can be offset if we have the right Congress, and that's the fastest thing to solve the problem.",
