  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "You are very astute supervisor. I grew up in Independence, Missouri. So my political hero is Harry S. Truman. And yes, my cat is named after that president. It's funny. I have officially now on my personal Facebook page. I still have sort of a normal official Facebook page, which is like Rep Huffman. You can just type that in and you'll get to my official Facebook page. But I've also had a personal and campaign side page for years. Facebook changed its algorithm. And I started noticing about six months ago, nobody was seeing my stuff on the personal side. And they kept giving me these notices that I could promote and boost my posts and get people to see them if I wanted to pay. And that's like total BS, I'm not gonna do that. So I have discovered that if I post cute pictures of my cat Truman, all of a sudden the metrics are the way they used to be. Everybody sees my post and, you know, we're back in business. So I have just officially rededicated my personal Facebook page to Truman. It's now called Congressman Huffman's cat Truman. And I hope people like cats.",
