    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 52,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, thanks, Dan. So the Noyo Center for those who don't know us, nonprofit here based in Fort Bragg, who we really work with marine science, conservation, and education. We have a couple interpretive facilities, the Discovery Center, downtown, and the crowsness on the headlands, but until this point we did not have any access to the water. And board members and staff at the Noyo Center had been looking at different properties in Noyo Harbor over the years, but nothing really fit what we're looking for. And then the idea came up to look at this former restaurant used to be Carini's Fish Grotto. Close in 2014 had been sitting empty since then. And a lot of people are asking like, why did you guys get a restaurant? And you know, even some of the staff had those thoughts too, but it gives us 60 feet of dock access to the river and gets us onto the river in which we can talk about, which really is a game changer for us and really helps in all of our marine science work and research and education programs we're doing.",
