    "turn_idx": 54,
    "turn_text": "Right, so I'd been following what the Noyo Center for Marine Science has been doing from afar. My husband and I moved from Indiana in 2019 and we're really interested in what was happening here. And shortly after moving here I started volunteering with the organization and really fell in love with the mission and the people and the tenacity of the people involved and the Can Do attitude with this organization. And so when the opportunity came around for them to hire an operations manager, I submitted my resume and was fortunate enough to get the job just a year ago, August of 2021. So I've just been here about a year and I'm so happy to be a part of the organization. I'm here as the operations manager helping to basically facilitate anything that needs to happen from developing policies and working with staff on HR and navigating insurance and paying bills and all that that kind of helps support what the organization is doing so that our amazing staff can do what they do.",
