  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's for those who haven't been here. I would tell you to come down and just experience it, but it is incredible. Like even right now, as we've been sitting here out on the deck that overlooks the river, we see sea lions, harbor seals, river otters, and a variety of birds in this area. So it's just like this front row view for all the rich marine life and animals that we have in this harbor and also you get to see a working harbor. You get to see fishing boats go by tour groups and see all the activity that this harbor really provides both this community, tourists that come in. So we're thrilled to have the space people just been raving about coming out here and getting to have coffee, some food. some drinks and just getting to enjoy the space and feel more connected to the natural world at this wonderful place where they get to see these animals up close and get to learn more about what we're doing for the local area and for the Mendocino coast.",
