  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 60,
    "turn_text": "Alright, so we have this fantastic summer camp program that's headed up by Sue Coulter, our education coordinator and newer staff, Michael Bredow, who came on to help out with the camps and is also helping out with some other educational programs. So this past year we had four separate camps and they all almost all of them sold out within weeks. They're a really popular way for kids to engage with nature and experience a lot of different activities and make new friends and we've had several repeat customers, kids who had such a great time over the last couple years and they wanted to come back and it's been a really good program and we're definitely wanting to continue that but then expand on that using the harbor property as also another educational point. I also wanted to talk about a little bit with the cafe and the way that that allows us to engage are the community at a whole different level. So coming in for a cup of coffee or some great food, they can also experience some of our staff who are here on site who are knowledgeable about marine science. And you never know who might be here or maybe what kind of projects we're working on, but anybody coming in can come in and engage with our staff and learn about what's going on kind of spontaneously. But we also do plan on having some science talks and more organized events out here to utilize the harbor in that way as an educational platform.",
