  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 71,
    "turn_text": "And again, this is your third building that you have your your staffing with volunteers and paid staff. here in Fort Bragg. This is the first one. On the waterfront in Noyo Harbor, you have the facility on Main Street in Fort Bragg, pretty much across from the Guest House Museum. And then you've got on the crow's nest out on the Fort Bragg, Noyo Headlands on property that the city of Fort Bragg and the Coastal Conservancy helped acquire. And I know that you have plans for an additional site on that campus on the headlands. Can you talk a little bit about what that final facility would look like? It's a major undertaking that it's pretty ambitious. Where it looks to me, the plans I've seen look like a world-class museum purpose-built facility. Can you talk a little bit about the planning for that?",
