    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "yeah yeah literally touched on it um you know the the ocean science center you're right the plans it's ambitious it's not only would house the blue whale skeleton it would have some large aquariums um it would have space for labs for make maker spaces it would have a cafe that would be bigger than this one down here um plus a lot of other exhibits so it's ambitious and i really see you know talking about the three facilities we have right now I'm really seeing this like nice progression where each spot while all connected kind of are helping us build a piece of that puzzle what will need to be to run that place. You know, we have the interpretive facilities where we have the exhibits, which will be such a large centerpiece on a bigger scale at the center. Now we have this place on the river where we can start doing, we can ramp up our research. We can see how to run a cafe. We can do that piece of getting people more engaged, which will be a large part of that, like building up lab space, both for local folks, but for research teams I want to come from outside the area so all these different pieces are helping us kind of learn those tools so we are better equipped when it comes time for that capital push to build a center where we know how to run all the different elements that it'll take to do something like that and be a big draw in this community.",
