  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so I could address that really quickly. I think one of our next steps is to get a change of use permit for this facility. So here at the cafe, We're operating under the previous permit because it was a restaurant, but we need a change of use permit in order to do some more of our research programs that we have planned. Like Michael had mentioned, the abalone broodstock program, which we plan to have here at the harbor and the purple urchin project, which will ideally allow us to work with local fishermen to collect purple urchin that are a problem in the ocean right now with creating those urchin barons and destroying the kelp forests. because the ocean is out of balance. So we're hoping to be able to collect these purple urchin and basically raise them, feed them, and then provide a potential food source and product for our community restaurants to be able to serve purple urchin uni. So that's another thing that's in the works as far as research and allowing this change of use permit will allow us to do more of the research side of things from the harbor.",
