  {
    "episode_id": 43939,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43939.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "Oh yeah, our volunteers do a little bit of everything. And I'm glad you brought them up because this cafe would not be open right now if it's not for hundreds of hours of volunteer work from painting deck to scrubbing kitchen equipment to everything. But our volunteers will be everything. One of the main ones, we have docents that keep up the crowsness out on the heavens. That's actually all volunteer led out there. They come in, speak with guests coming in, give them a relay of the land there. We have beach survey teams that go out to different beaches throughout Mendocino County, tracking, and kind of tracking numbers, keeping an eye on the different type of plant life, animal life, they're seeing there. This year we've had volunteers also help us with a sea star program where we've been going out once a month during minus tides looking for any evidence of sunflower sea stars, which disappeared from the coast some years ago and were a main predator of the Purple Urchin. there were some evidence that maybe some juvenile ones were seeing the spring so we've been going out to low tide looking for any evidence in those tide pools. We also have volunteers help us when there's community events. If we have tables and booths set up trying to engage with the public they'll be out there for that. You know helping us you know just down here you know with Clean up work like that. We'll be doing part of the community cleanup piece later this month, and it will volunteers help there. So that's just some of the stuff they do, and it'll continue to be evolving. We're especially down here when we kind of get an idea of where we can use volunteers in this new space on the harbor. And I would say people interested can go to our website, sign up, see some of the different tasks, but also if people have a ticker skill set, always to let us know because there's places maybe we're not seeing that we could use help. I'm in the fundraising grant writing world and maybe there's people with really great copywriting skills. Different pieces, places that maybe we're not even thinking of using. We have one volunteer who does a lot of things but one thing she does is she's cooked up some really yummy goodies and has helped us sometimes at just like little events and receptions we have like to do that so it can be a real wide variety of things.",
